// python/references_w: the Python reference graph from W's Rust, core.rerail's reference_def, reference_edge and
// reference_open as python/references.rerail derives them by rules (decision 0483), for comparing the two.
//
// The engine builds the graph as W did (6970a3e539): each Python file summarized from its tape as the run builds its
// document (`calls::summarize`), the summaries linked once every file is built (`Graph::link_references`), under the
// program's `.references` setting (its sibling links, constructor fields and scope; none: every .py and .pyi file).
// It binds the two inputs below in the cross-file part (`logic::plan::corpus::w_references`).
//
// A program includes this file in place of python/references.rerail, or a run maps that include here with
// RERAIL_REFERENCES=rust (`rr::include_switched`): the program is otherwise the same, so the two runs differ only in
// how the graph is made.
//
// The graph is by symbol, as the rules' is (decision 0677: no node crosses into the cross-file part). The engine names
// each definition as rf_sym does, from W's own summary: its file's path, its qualified name, and how many of the file's
// definitions of that name start before it. A file's definitions get their symbols from the rules both graphs read
// (python/reference-defs.rerail's reference_def).

// The engine's inputs, by each definition's symbol as python/reference-defs.rerail's rf_sym spells it (`path:q#k`,
// decision 0677): no node crosses into the cross-file part, where the engine binds them. Each is derived there
// `cross_file` (decision 0652): its rows join definitions of any files. An input is per-document to the split whatever
// it is declared; its one reader here, derived across files, keeps it in the cross-file part, as the rules' graph is
// derived there.
#include "python/reference-defs.rerail"

.decl w_reference_edge(src: symbol, dst: symbol, via: symbol)
.decl w_reference_open(s: symbol)
.input w_reference_edge, w_reference_open
.decl w_edge(src: symbol, dst: symbol, via: symbol) cross_file
w_edge(s, d, v) :- w_reference_edge(s, d, v).
.decl w_open(s: symbol) cross_file
w_open(s) :- w_reference_open(s).

reference_edge(s, d, v) :- w_edge(s, d, v).
reference_open(s) :- w_open(s).
